WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.970
A second frost.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:09.910
In 1798, another poem's speaker sits indoors by a low fire, a baby asleep beside him.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.350
Outside: The Frost performs its secret ministry.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.850
In 1900, Hardy's speaker leans on a gate: When Frost was spectre-gray.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.300
Two poems, one cold.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.670
In an exam, the question says: compare.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.310
So how do you compare two winter poems?

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:38.070
In this mission, you'll read the opening and ending of Coleridge's Frost at Midnight, and set the two frosts side by side.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.290
You'll find out what examiners reward, and learn how to put the two poems together.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.390
Your mission: find out how to compare two winter poems.
